# Map element `code.catalog.model`: OpenRouter model selection — proposed corrected description

This draft applies the resolutions (GF1–GF9) to the element description. Changes are noted
inline. It is a proposal for discussion; the decisions themselves live in `resolution.md`.

## Properties
```json
{
  "package": "agent host library (reusable; basis for the chassis)",
  "name": "OpenRouter model selection",
  "name_length": 2,
  "role": "SE",
  "uri": "crates/acp-host/src/models.rs; crates/roundtable-web/src/app.rs (/api/models route); crates/roundtable-web/assets/index.html (selection UI)"
}
```
_GF5: uri broadened to cover the route and the page, not just models.rs._

## What other parts rely on it for (their wants)
- `code.roster.participant` (beneficiary) ← the chair (who picks participants by OpenRouter
  model id), served by the web page: goal: Offer the OpenRouter models a participant can use.
  Function: Lists current OpenRouter model ids. Intent: receive.
_GF9: explicitly chains the web page → chair → participant, and defines chair (the user
operating the page) and seat (a participant slot whose harness runs the chosen model)._

## What it relies on (its wants)
- `upstream.gateway.llm`: goal: Obtain the current list of selectable models instead of a
  fixed list. Function: Publishes model identifiers and metadata through
  GET https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/models. Auth: Bearer key optional; taken from
  OPENROUTER_API_KEY or set via POST /api/settings. **The same key is also forwarded to every
  running table as the `SetJevKey` evaluator credential (app.rs:239) — catalog auth and the
  judge share one value.** Refresh: per page-load fetch; no server-side caching. Intent: receive.
_GF8 + peer-verified dual-role key: host, auth (incl. shared JEV role), and refresh/caching
cadence now stated._

## Layer `references`
```json
[
  {
    "path": "README.md",
    "sections": [ "9.4 OpenRouter Support" ]
  }
]
```

## Layer `elephant` (the project author's account of this element)
```json
{
  "date": "2026-11-07",
  "design": "Let the chair pick participants by OpenRouter model id from OpenRouter's live catalog, not a fixed list.",
  "sources": [ "README.md §9.4" ],
  "built": "acp-host/src/models.rs reads the catalog (endpoint, optional bearer key shared with the SetJevKey evaluator credential, keeps id/name/context_length); the web page offers a free-text model input with datalist hints drawn from the live catalog per page load; the typed id is not validated against the catalog. The chosen id becomes the session's generic 'model' option; if the harness does not advertise it, only a warning is recorded and the seat still joins.",
  "gaps": [
    "No filtering by ACP tool-use capability: all catalog models are offered (GF6).",
    "No failure behavior documented: on catalog/auth failure /api/models returns 502 and the page silently degrades to an empty input (GF2, GF7).",
    "No fixed fallback list by design (GF7)."
  ]
}
```
_GF1: built now states the free-text+datalist mechanism instead of "the web page lists the
models". GF3: how the selection is used is now stated. GF6/GF2/GF7: gaps are now explicit
rather than absent._
